

**Derivatives With Respect to Order**

**10.1.41**

\[\begin{array}{l}\left[\frac{\partial}{\partial p}j_{\gamma}(x)\right]_{n=0}=( \frac{1}{2}\pi/x)\left(\mathrm{Ci}(2x)\,\sin\,x-\mathrm{Si}(2x)\,\cos\,x\right) \\ \\ \left[\frac{\partial}{\partial p}\,j_{\gamma}(x)\right]_{n=1}=(1\pi/x)\left\{ \mathrm{Ci}(2x)\,\cos\,x+\mathrm{Si}(2x)\,\sin\,x\right\}\\ \\ \left[\frac{\partial}{\partial p}\,j_{\gamma}(x)\right]_{n=0}=(1\pi/x)\left\{ \mathrm{Ci}(2x)\,\cos\,x+\mathrm{[Si}(2x)-\pi]\sin x\right\}\\ \\ \left[\frac{\partial}{\partial p}\,j_{\gamma}(x)\right]_{n=1}=(\frac{1}{2}\pi/x) \left\{\mathrm{Ci}(2x)\,\sin\,x-\mathrm{[Si}(2x)-\pi]\cos\,x\right\}\\ \\ \end{array}\]

**10.1.44**

\[\begin{array}{l}\left[\frac{\partial}{\partial p}\,j_{\gamma}(x)\right]_{n=1} \equiv\\ \\ \left(\frac{3}{2}\pi/x\right)\left\{\mathrm{Ci}(2x)\,\sin\,x-\mathrm{[Si}(2x)- \pi]\cos\,x\right\}\\ \\ \end{array}\]

